From e9f868cb905dca49554d1b4d5441fa2b6b027763 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:34:47 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 27/28] VideoOutput: draw the views of a depth video on the
 GPU, the best way that keeps its frame rate

The views of a picture with its depth map are drawn with libstereo-dibr's GLSL passes in an OpenGL context of its own, on the GPU the
process draws with: the planes of 8 bit planar and semi-planar YUV frames are uploaded as they are and turned into RGBA by a pass
here, the frames of hardware decoders and of other formats arrive as RGBA images, and the full side by side frame is read back. The
context lives in a thread of its own, because the frames of a video reach VideoOutput from several threads and a context belongs to
one. The C code on the processor draws what the GPU does not read and what no OpenGL context can be made for, and the log of
qt.multimedia.video.depth says so, with the reason, whenever it changes.

The way (warping and gap filling) is automatic until the program picks one: the first way of libstereo-dibr's ladder whose slowest
frames fit four fifths of the frame's time on the GPU (or processor) that draws, timed once for each GPU and size and kept in the
person's cache. New properties: stereoDepthAutomatic, stereoDepthGpu, stereoDepthChoice, and the StereoDepthFillPyramid fill. The
defaults of the depth properties are read from libstereo-dibr's stereo_dibr_options_default().

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
